Since I've been struggling to get a character past Exp Lvl 10 I've been 
reading some tips online.  There are some that suggest that you stay on 
D-lvl 1 until you hit E-lvl 3 and then try to keep your E-lvl 1 above the 
D-lvl you're on.  Others suggest letting your pet kill everything on the 
first few levels to get up its hit points.  I'm not sure if these are 
mutually exclusive strategies, but here's the problem I'm having with both 
of them:  I don't tend to stay on a level I've already "cleared" for fear of 
running out of food.  I know I can pray for a meal, but I don't want to get 
in the habit of "wasting" prayers on food when I might need that prayer 
later, or if it won't solve the general problem.  I guess overall I have the 
impression that there aren't enough monsters re-spawning on a level I've 
cleared to warrant me sticking around very long.  I'm probably mistaken 
about that, but that's just the feeling I've gotten so far.  On average I 
find that I hit the E-lvl of a D-lvl shortly after I've started on that 
level, playing what I consider "comfortably".

So, what would you veteran players suggest?  Should I just suck it up and 
stick to a formula of not hitting the next D-lvl until I'm a E-lvl or two 
ahead of it, or will I find that a strategy like that will just leave me 
with a pile of starved corpses? 



